WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
A cell is preparing to send a protein beyond its boundary.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.500
Inside, a transport vesicle carries that cargo toward the surface.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.000
Its membrane keeps the protein separate from the cytoplasm.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Now it reaches the plasma membrane. But touching is not enough.

5
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Predict: can the protein escape before the membranes fuse?

6
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.500
Watch: the membranes merge, forming a passage to the outside.

7
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.500
Only then can the enclosed cargo move into the space beyond the cell.

8
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.000
This is exocytosis: release through membrane fusion.

9
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
What evidence showed that contact alone was not release?
